Well, I remember once accidentally destroying my bag of holding when I was
climbing the stairs from the Valley to the Castle with the amulet.
And I didn't have _any_ means of levitation or that hadn't been destroyed
with the bag, and no water walking boots or wands of cold either. 
Of course, the Castle wand also got destroyed, so I couldn't make a wish.
And I was on the wrong side of the Castle..
When I realized that, I really felt like #quitting there and then.
But I didn't. 

First I decided to try my luck with the trapdoors in the castle corridor,
knowing that every now and then the RNG decides that you can actually walk
over a trapdoor without falling through. After what felt like forever,
I finally managed to cross the first three trapdoors and got to the
treasure rooms. I checked the armor room, and saw there was no levitation
of water walking boots, either. Of course, when I tried to go further to
the West, I got dropped through the next trapdoor.
Then I finally believed that it will not work that way.

I dropped the Amulet at the Castle level (to prevent the Wizard from
reappearing) and jumped through the trapdoor to try to find some
levitation equipment from Gehennom.
I walked through every Gehennom level, didn't find any. Even the
guaranteed boots in Vlad's tower had been in the bag that exploded
earlier.
So I collected piles of armor, rings and potions in the Orcus level and
started polypiling. All I got was a potion of gain level (which some
monster kindly cursed later) and a potion of levitation (or was there
two.. I don't remember).

Anyway, I knew that cursed potions of gain level don't always work when
you're carrying the amulet, so when I reached the castle level, I didn't
yet pick up the amulet. Instead, I quaffed the cursed gain level without
it and descended the stairs. There were some boulders in front of the
castle. (I have a habit of making a tunnel of boulders in front of the
drawbridge.) I pushed those boulders to the trapdoors, filling all but the
last one of them. Stepped on the last hole, found myself on the Valley
again, so up the stairs, pick up the amulet.. and with only one trapdoor
left, it didn't take too long to get to the other side.
I saved the potion of levitation to the Air level, and finally ascended
that game.

